## Python Instruction
Write a function to check if a given string is a special-equivalent string. A string is special-equivalent if it can be transformed into another string by swapping any two even indexed characters or any two odd indexed characters.

## Python Solution
```python
def is_special_equivalent(str1, str2):
    if len(str1) != len(str2):
        return False
    odd_str1 = ''.join(sorted(str1[1::2]))
    even_str1 = ''.join(sorted(str1[::2]))
    odd_str2 = ''.join(sorted(str2[1::2]))
    even_str2 = ''.join(sorted(str2[::2]))
    return odd_str1 == odd_str2 and even_str1 == even_str2
```

## Python Tests
assert is_special_equivalent("zzxy", "xyzz") == True
assert is_special_equivalent("abcd", "cdab") == True
assert is_special_equivalent("zzxy", "zzyx") == False

## Canonical Elixir names (use verbatim)
- Module: `Solution`
- Function: `special_equivalent?`

